  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Although ::1 has been verified to work in IPv6 environments (see ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-581#icft=FCREPO-581"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": "), the default policies deny-apim-if-not-localhost and deny-reloadPolicies-if-not-localhost will not work as expected (authorization fails) in environments where the client IP address comes in as a long-form IPv6 loopback address.  The long form of the IPv6 loopback address is 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1, and can also be provided as 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1%0 (the latter is the case on my mac, when using Firefox to hit a local Fedora repository instance).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "These default policies should be updated to work in such cases.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
