  "description": "<p>Although ::1 has been verified to work in IPv6 environments (see \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-581\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-581\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Default XACML policies involving localhost don&#39;t work in IPv6 environments\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-581\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n), the default policies deny-apim-if-not-localhost and deny-reloadPolicies-if-not-localhost will not work as expected (authorization fails) in environments where the client IP address comes in as a long-form IPv6 loopback address.  The long form of the IPv6 loopback address is 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1, and can also be provided as 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1%0 (the latter is the case on my mac, when using Firefox to hit a local Fedora repository instance).</p>\n\n<p>These default policies should be updated to work in such cases.</p>",
